    <statement><p>Evaluate the line integral
<m>\int_C 7 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy</m> where <m>C</m> is the
straight line path from <m>(3,1)</m> to <m>(8, 6)</m>.</p>
<p><m>\int_C 7 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy =</m> <fillin characters="45" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>7\cdot \left(\frac{6-1}{2}+1\right)\mathopen{}\left(8-3\right)+2\cdot \left(\frac{8-3}{2}+3\right)\mathopen{}\left(6-1\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>C</m>:
<me>x= 3 + 5 t, \qquad y = 1 + 5 t, \qquad 0\le t \le 1,</me>
so that  <m>dx= 5\, dt</m> and <m>dy = 5\,dt</m>.  Hence
<me>\int_C 7 y \, dx + 2 x \, dy =
\int_0^1 7(1 + 5 t)5\, dt + 2(3 + 5 t)5\, dt =
\int_0^1 65 + 225 t\, dt = 177.5.</me>



</solution>
